{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-30T18:01:02.166Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. All acceptance lines are implemented and both verifies pass.\n\n## Summary\n\n**New module** `src/core/spec/checkout-draft.ts`:\n- `removeCheckoutDraft(vcs, projectRoot, folderPath)` — removes the folder unless `vcs.pathExists('HEAD', <repo-relative path>)` is true.\n- `restoreStackedDraft(projectRoot, config, change)` — copies a stacked copy into the checkout, replaces any existing folder, prunes `.run/` except `manifest.json` and `plan.jsonl`, leaves the stacked dir untouched, returns the absolute path.\n\n**Wired in**:\n- `approve-worktree.ts`: `removeCheckoutDraft` after the worktree commit and after `recordStackedApproval`; 247 lines, no other change.\n- `approve.ts`: a stacked change is restored and approved like a checkout draft; the whole path runs in a try/catch that removes the restored draft and rethrows on any failure (declined confirmation included); the old `not found` refusal for stacked changes is gone.\n- `reject.ts` / `cli/reject.ts`: stacked rejection restores the draft before deleting the stacked dir, returns `restoredPath`, and prints `  Restored draft: <path>`.\n\n**Tests**: new `tests/approve-owns-draft.test.ts` covers all five delta scenarios plus the lint-failing stacked re-approval; `approve-worktree`, `approve-stacked`, and `reject-worktree` were updated to read worktree/stacked copies, expect the checkout draft gone, and expect the restored draft.\n\n**Verification**:\n- Task verify `node --import tsx --test tests/approve-owns-draft.test.ts` — 6/6 pass.\n- Proposal verify `pnpm verify` — exit 0 (2850 + 94 tests, 0 fail; typechecks, build, lint clean).\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/123-approve-owns-draft/.run/results/3.md`."}}
